@startuml
title V6 production candidate: explicit turn-cardinality precheck
top to bottom direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

artifact "prompt + candidate response\n(no id, label, explanation)" as Input
component "Lossless event parser\nsystem / user / assistant / tool" as Parser
component "Exact checks\ntool schema + explicit system rules" as Exact
diamond "Explicit one-call or\ntext-XOR-call rule violated?" as Gate
component "Frozen one-shot semantic path\nevidence reader + LLM + strict claim gate" as LLM
artifact "label 1\nexact rule and action spans" as Positive
artifact "semantic decision\nor fallback 0" as Output

Input --> Parser
Parser --> Exact
Exact --> Gate
Gate --> Positive : yes\n(no LLM call)
Gate --> LLM : no
LLM --> Output

note right of Gate
  Multiple calls are not inherently errors.
  The check activates only from an
  authoritative system-policy sentence.
  User text cannot create the rule.
end note

note bottom of Positive
  Full 46-row replay:
  TP 16, FP 5, FN 7, TN 18
  F1 0.7273 (baseline 0.6667)
  35 vs 40 logical LLM calls
end note
@enduml
